  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nCyclonic flow aloft will continue through today with a surface\ntrough swinging across the area early this afternoon. This bring\nchances for isolated showers while much of the area will\nexperience partly to mostly sunny skies today. Hi res guidance\nhas backed off a bit on the wind fields while mixing to around\n700 mb seems likely. Mean momentum transfer is around 25 kts\nwith winds at the top of the mixed layer are 30-35 kts. This\nwill likely translate to peak gusts around 30 mph with sporadic\nhigher gusts. There will also be potential for higher gusts with\nany sustained shower.\n\nHigh pressure builds in Friday night into Saturday that will\nallow gusty winds to subside Friday night. Saturday will be a\npleasant day with sunny skies and high temperatures ranging \nfrom the upper 40s near the Canadian Border to low 60s south of \nthe mountains. The center of the high will drift into the Gulf \nof Maine Saturday night while it will still likely provide \nfavorable conditions for radiational cooling. This will likely \nlead to lows dropping below freezing for much of the interior \nwith frost potential all the way to the coast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\n\nLatest forecast guidance continues to indicate that remnant moisture \nfrom Tropical Cyclone Isaias will bring a period of rainfall to the \narea late Sunday into Monday morning. Rainfall amounts will likely \nbe light with amounts ranging from around 1/2\" across portions of \nsouthern NH and southwestern ME to less than 1/10\" of an inch across \nnorthern locations. Partial clearing is likely later Monday with \nabove avg high temperatures into the upper 60s/low 70s south of the \nmtns. \n\nAfter a warm Monday night, a cold front and associated wave of low \npressure will cross from the north on Tuesday. This will bring \nanother period of showery weather and gusty SW winds before turning \nto the NW Tuesday night as CAA increases behind the front. Cooler \ntemperatures will then prevail mid to late week with mainly dry \nconditions.",
